  "worked_solution": "The support of $X$ is ${S}_{X}={0,1},$ the support of $Y$ is ${S}_{Y}={1,2,3},$ and therefore the joint support $S$ is\n\n$$\nS={S}_{X}\\times {S}_{Y}={(0,1),(0,2),(0,3),(1,1),(1,2),(1,3)}.\n$$\n\nSince we're given a joint probability distribution $f(x,y),$ we must have \n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}f(x,y)=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(0,1)+f(0,2)+f(0,3)+f(1,1)+f(1,2)+f(1,3) & =1 \\\\ a+2a+a+3a+a+2a & =1 \\\\ 10a & =1 \\\\ a & =\\frac{1}{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
